# A rule that can never complete (every alternative needs itself) is
# rejected: no input derives it, and LALR lookaheads assume every rule can.
# error: unproductive_rule.grammar:19:
# error: loop derives no finite input
@lexer
tokens
    ident
    comma
    eof
    err
','                                         → comma
[a-zA-Z]+                                   → ident
.                                           → err
@parser
@conflicts = 0
program! = item                             → 1
item     = IDENT
         | loop
loop     = loop "," IDENT                   → (loop 1 3)
